The Go rendering: a command that overwrites a variable before a closure naming it
is written, stores to a variable after a closure naming it is written, and does
both inside a loop, where the closure of one iteration precedes the stores of the
next, and stores after a closure it calls where it writes it and after one it starts
in a goroutine.

